{
  "_doc": "Compact SBS metric policy shared by run_eval.py and the report. A baseline movement is a regression only when it exceeds max(abs_floor, baseline*rel_tol). Hard bounds are non-tradeable. scope separates perceptual candidates from renderer conformance, GT-only validation, and temporal-only evaluation. Model-label export remains fail closed: only label_status=qualified is learnable; all current candidates are experimental.",
  "_scope_note": "perceptual risk metrics may become DA-V2 augmentation labels after controlled-corruption and headset validation. Stereo volume is a style descriptor, not an unbounded reward: select the strongest scale only after independent safety/coherence/artifact constraints pass. conformance metrics catch renderer/transport contract bugs and are never perceptual labels. gt-only metrics require authenticated reference depth/disparity or an authored subtitle region. temporal-only metrics evaluate sequences and are not single-frame policy labels.",
  "_comfort_note": "Disparity percentages are normalized image disparity, not retinal angle. The existing +/-3% tails and over-limit burden are retained as experimental safety heuristics until calibrated for a fixed display FOV and headset/user study.",
